Glucose should be measured immediately after collection, otherwise the blood sample should be collected into a container with glycolytic inhibitors, immediately centrifuged to separate the plasma, and frozen until analysis.

- · In asymptomatic people, repeat the test to confirm the diagnosis, preferably with the same test, as soon as practicable on a subsequent day.
- · If plasma glucose ≥18 mmol/L (325 mg/dL), or symptoms are present, measure urine ketones to assess degree of metabolic disturbance.
- · If plasma glucose measurement is not possible, urine glucose testing can be used to confirm suspicion of diabetes in people with symptoms. A negative urine test does not exclude diabetes, but it excludes severe hyperglycaemia.

